 "_curve": "HEALTH ON THE BOARD PER WAVE, which is the curve tests/content.test.ts measures rather than the body count: 576, 864, 1245, 1727, 2175, 3045, 3348, 4480, 5352, 6439, 6742, 7500, 7552, 8630, 9200, 10258, 11430, and then the boss wave's 3559 escort. EVERY STEP IS POSITIVE AND NONE IS OVER 55%, which are the two halves of that rule; the boss wave is exempt from the first, which is what a boss is for.\nTHE FOUR CALLBACK WAVES ARE THE AWKWARD ONES and they are why the callbacks rise in health. A wave that is one mini boss plus an escort has to be heavier than the forty-body wave before it, so either the callbacks get fatter in the order they arrive or the escorts do -- and an escort large enough to carry the curve past a 2900 hp Politician is fifty bodies walking round a fight the player is supposed to be watching. Level 9 answered the same question the same way: 650, 3100, 3400, 8100 across its four. The first draft here had the four flat and dipped 43% at wave 13."
